-- title:
--   Unbounded-cap original stopped negative-mark integral has a uniform count majorant and integrable count
-- statement:
--   The source physical negative-mark integral J n on the strict preterminal and ruin mask is uniformly bounded in absolute value by K times the original finite-horizon negative-mark count. The count is integrable since negative-jump activity is finite. Unlike finite-cap phys50, the dividend cap is top and the argument uses the newly Proved compact value loss and prepayment reserve envelope.
-- source:
--   Exact topcap replacement of Proved finite-cap phys50 9a6793e4. The source count L1 lemma phys51 1d9db509 is cap-free. The topcap kernel absolute bound is public helper 6b6d3ac9; the supported integral bound phys54 is Proved.

